from parts/safari-enter.replay
# sys-safari-retire (docs/research/great-marsh.md): three steps on the marsh's plain ground count as Safari steps
# (Field_UpdateSafari; no encounters there). The start menu in a Safari Game: RETIRE first, SAVE hidden, the ball
# window. RETIRE (SAFARI_GAME 21): "Would you like to exit?", YES: the warp back to the gate's north door facing
# south, VAR_SAFARI_GAME_STATE 2 and start_end_safari_game 1; the gate's on-frame script (state 2) walks the player
# five steps south and sets the state back to 0.
+0 press up
until position 68 113
+0 release up
until idle
+0 assert state safari.steps 3
+0 press x
+1 release x
until app start-menu
+0 assert app start-menu
+1 tap entry:0
until yesno
+0 assert text platinum:SafariGame_Text_WouldYouLikeToExit 0
+0 press a
+1 release a
until idle
+0 assert position platinum:MAP_HEADER_PASTORIA_CITY_OBSERVATORY_GATE_1F 5 7
+0 assert facing player down
+0 assert flag platinum:FLAG_SAFARI_GAME_ACTIVE false
+0 assert var platinum:VAR_SAFARI_GAME_STATE 0
+0 assert state safari {"balls":0,"steps":0,"caught":0}
